From fbc2ea73f93087ef91bb7963f5d047fe9b21468f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: PolyOpenFirmware <alex.camilo@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 1 Jul 2026 15:32:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 8/9] ASoC: add C60 audio machine driver

Add a machine driver (poly,c60-audio) for the Poly Trio C60 (i.MX 8M
Mini "Kepler"). One snd_soc_card exposes BOTH directions of SAI1 as two
DAI links that share the single fsl_sai DAI:

  link 0  "Speaker"    cpu=SAI1  codec  = TAS5751M            (playback)
  link 1  "Mic Array"  cpu=SAI1  codecs = 3x TLV320ADC3101    (capture)

The C60 wires SAI1 RX hard-synced to TX (no RX_BCLK/RX_SYNC pads), so
the SAI is the sole bit-clock and frame provider for both directions and
every codec is a pure clock consumer. The driver therefore fixes the DAI
format in C to I2S | NB_NF | CBC_CFC on both links.

This fixed format is the whole reason a machine driver is needed instead
of a DT-only audio-graph-card2 card: graph-card2 hands the primary ADC a
mixed bit/frame clock role, and tlv320adc3xxx only accepts a full
provider (CBP_CFP) or full consumer (CBC_CFC) role, bailing out of
adc3xxx_set_dai_fmt() with -EINVAL ("Invalid DAI clock setup").

The three ADCs each present a stereo I2S pair on their own SAI RX data
line (RXD0/1/2); the SAI de-interleaves the three lanes into one
6-channel capture stream via its MULTI_SAI DMA. The capture link's
hw_params programs 2 TDM slots on the CPU DAI so the SAI splits the
stream across 3 data lanes (pins = DIV_ROUND_UP(channels, slots) = 3),
and announces the 24.576 MHz MCLK to each ADC so tlv320adc3xxx can
resolve a PLL/divider table entry.

Codecs are resolved from DT phandle lists (poly,audio-cpu,
poly,audio-dac-codec, poly,audio-adc-codec); optional DAPM widgets and
routing come from poly,widgets / poly,routing.

Signed-off-by: Poly Open Firmware <alex.camilo@gmail.com>
---
 sound/soc/fsl/Kconfig     |  16 ++
 sound/soc/fsl/Makefile    |   2 +
 sound/soc/fsl/c60-audio.c | 368 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 386 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 sound/soc/fsl/c60-audio.c

diff --git a/sound/soc/fsl/Kconfig b/sound/soc/fsl/Kconfig
index 725c530a3..2996f5fcc 100644
--- a/sound/soc/fsl/Kconfig
+++ b/sound/soc/fsl/Kconfig
@@ -381,6 +381,22 @@ config SND_SOC_IMX_CARD
 	  with OF-graph DT bindings.
 	  It also support DPCM of single CPU multi Codec ststem.
 
+config SND_SOC_C60_AUDIO
+	tristate "SoC Audio support for the Poly Trio C60 (Kepler)"
+	depends on OF && I2C
+	select SND_SOC_FSL_SAI
+	select SND_SOC_IMX_PCM_DMA
+	select SND_SOC_TAS571X
+	select SND_SOC_TLV320ADC3XXX
+	help
+	  Machine driver for the Poly Trio C60 (i.MX 8M Mini "Kepler"): a
+	  single sound card exposing TAS5751M speaker playback and a
+	  3 x TLV320ADC3101 microphone-array capture, both on SAI1. The
+	  driver fixes the DAI format to I2S / CBC_CFC in C (SAI is the sole
+	  clock provider) which the codecs accept where audio-graph-card2's
+	  mixed clock role does not.
+	  Say Y if you are building for the Poly Trio C60.
+
 endif # SND_IMX_SOC
 
 endmenu
